
    In __init__.py for whole fptk I have option to always import monads/strict/lens.
    In normal fptk I don't use it.
    But I usually use it in projects with fptk_local (because I don't want to write "(import lens *)" in every proj file).

// How to use fptk_local in projs ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾\ {{{1

    ## In non-package (without __init__ or smth) proj:

        Just place whole /fptk_local dir in app.hy folder (or whatever top file is called)
        And import it as (import fptk_local *)

        All inner imports should use this name too "(import fptk_local.core.funcs *)"
        // fptk_local_generator takes care of these renamings

    ## In package proj (for example "wy"):

        Example:
        - project is called "wy" and is pip-installed (pip install -e .)
        - fptk_local is at /wy/utils/fptk_local folder

        Then:
        - place whole /fptk_local dir in /wy/utils folder
        - inner imports should be used like this: "(import wy.utils.fptk_local.core.funcs *)"

        All inner imports should follow this rule too: "(import wy.utils.fptk_local.core.funcs *)"
        // fptk_local_generator can be used for this

// ____________________________________________________________________________/ }}}1
// Macros hy.R issue ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾\ {{{1

    for macro f> and similar they internally use:
    hy.R.fptk_local.core.macros.fm

    - for vanilla fptk:
        ✓ (hy.R.fptk.core.macros.fm (+ it 1)) — works
        ± (fm (+ it 1)) — works, but in order for f> to work, fm has to be imported too

    - for fptk_local in non-package proj:
        ✓ (hy.R.fptk_local.core.macros.fm (+ it 1)) — works
        ± (fm (+ it 1)) — same as for vanilla fptk

    - for fptk_local in package proj (using same wy-proj example):
        ✗ (hy.R.wy.utils.fptk_local.core.macros.fm (+ it 1)) — does NOT work (but probably need some proper imports)
        ± (fm (+ it 1)) — same as for vanilla fptk

        for this reason I use second (which is ±) option for wy
        meh, but hey

// ____________________________________________________________________________/ }}}1
// Macros issue — old note ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾\ {{{1

    when only importing (import fptk [f>]), f> is required to have fm internally, and it can be called as:

    -> hy.R.fptk.fm               -> ✗ does not work in dev file
                                     ✓ works from outside projs (it is essentially call to installed lib)
                                     ✓ this is how it is done in hyrule (I think this is due to their hy_init.hy importing everything)

       fm                         -> [✓ ✗] works from dev file
       hy.R.fptk_macros.fm        -> [✓ ✗] works from dev file
       hy.R.fptk.fptk_macros.fm   -> [✗ ✗] does not work anywhere


// ____________________________________________________________________________/ }}}1

